{
  "_comment": "Catalog of raw side effects -- the only place for the declaration. hy-index (Rust) takes it in at build time (include_str!) and emits raw (the fact of raw side-effect evidence) for each definition. It makes no rule verdicts (the source of truth for verdicts is the linter in agora-controllers). The VS Code extension only displays this fact and holds no catalog. A pattern matches by prefix on the full name resolved through imports at a segment boundary (a trailing * is a prefix match within a segment); a builtin is counted only for an unimported, unqualified name at the head position of a call; a method is matched by method name alone and counted only when the context module appears in the file's imports or in a reference inside the definition. ignored lists names that match a pattern but are not side effects.",
  "strength": {
    "pattern": "strong",
    "builtin": "strong",
    "method": "weak"
  },
